\label{wk} Let $\{v(n)\}$ be a sequence of elements of closed interval $[a,b],$\newline $a<b$. Suppose that $F$ is continuous non decreasing function such that $F(a)=0, F(b)=1$. Then $F$ is the asymptotic distribution function of $\{v(n)\}$ if and if
\begin{equation}
\label{WKI}
\lim_{N\to \infty} E_N(f(v))= \int_a^b f(x)dF(x)
\end{equation}
for each continuous function $f$ defined on $[a,b]$.

\label{pcontalgebra}
The system of the sets of $P$ - continuity
$\mathcal{B}_c(M)$ is an algebra of sets.
